{# The turn's anchor, written once into history and read from there for the
   rest of the thread. Facts only: no countdown, because a countdown is true
   for a minute and this line is not rewritten. A row outlives the model that
   wrote it, so it renders the same at every guidance level and takes no
   guidance kwarg. Every line is guarded, so an unsupplied value drops its
   line instead of rendering a blank.

   The lines carry no labels. A stamp, a session line and a gap each say what
   they are in their own words, so a label would only spend tokens naming what
   the line already names. The run line keeps its words because "web, AAPL,
   automation" is not self-describing; it just loses its heading, and its
   first letter is raised so it reads as a sentence whichever piece leads.

   `market_line` is supplied only when the market state moved since the last
   row that stated it (see `TurnContextMiddleware._market_line`), so an absent
   line here means unchanged, which `components/time_rules.md.j2` tells the
   model. `surface_rules` is the one steering block a row carries, rendered by
   `envelope/surface_rules.md.j2` and supplied only when this turn's delivery
   rules are not the last ones still on the wire, which is why it is a whole
   paragraph rather than a line. `disk_recovered` is set on the first turn
   after a row that stated the low-disk line, since that line stays in history
   in the present tense and would otherwise still read as standing. #}
